<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bissandugu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bissandugu is a town in the Kankan region of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> that served as the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samori-ture">Samori Ture</a>'s Wassoulou Empire from the 1870s. In 1887 Samori and the French signed a treaty there that recognised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> as the boundary between their territories. French troops captured the town in 1891 during their campaigns against Samori, who then moved his state eastwards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bissandugu.jpg" alt="Bissandugu" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lancine.kounfantoh.fofana · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%DF%95%DF%8E%DF%AC%DF%93%DF%8A%DF%AC%DF%93%DF%8E%DF%AC_%DF%9D%DF%8A%DF%9F%DF%8A%DF%B2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
